<blockquote class="uncited"><div>This is the reason it would be great to get OpenGD into it.</div></blockquote>Thats because the <span style="font-size:150%;line-height:116%">DR</span>-1801 is nothing at all like the DM-1801 or the DM-1701 or the GD-77 or the UV-380 or the MD-2017 etc.<br><br>The  <span style="font-size:150%;line-height:116%">DR</span>-1801 uses a sealed DMR module, which is also used in some mobile phones, and this module contains all transceiver and the microprocessor etc<br><br>The only other things on the PCB apart from this module, is the RF PA and the Rx preamps, which need to be physically large as they must have wound coil inductors and strip line PCB tracks etc.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Sat Sep 28, 2024 1:41 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
